---
{% from "plate.njk" import img, note %}
{% set heroPlate = atlas.places | findBySlug("fiordland") | attr("plate") %}

<section class="hero hero--short">
  {{ img(heroPlate, "wide", true) }}
  <span class="hero__scrim"></span>
  {{ note(heroPlate) }}
  <div class="hero__body">
    <p class="kicker hero__kicker">About</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">Hi, I'm <em>Ali</em></h1>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
  <div class="duo">
    <div>{{ img(atlas.places | findBySlug("eryri") | attr("plate"), "port", false, "(min-width:64rem) 38vw, 92vw") }}</div>
    <div class="duo__text">
      <p class="kicker">The short version</p>
      <h2 class="sec__title">I pay for <em>every night</em> I write about</h2>
      <p class="sec__sub">
        Nobody sponsors this and there are no affiliate links anywhere on it,
        which is the only reason some of the write-ups are lukewarm. If a place
        was crowded, overpriced or simply worse than the one an hour down the
        road, that is what the review says.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec sec--tint">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>How the scoring works</h2>
    <p>
      Five points, answering one question: would I tell someone else to go? It
      is not a measure of how nice somewhere is. A place can be spectacular and
      score three because it is crowded, overpriced, or better a hundred miles
      further on.
    </p>

    <h2>About the pictures</h2>
    <p>
      Some pages carry real photographs, all of them mine, all taken where
      they say they were. The rest still carry a <span class="flag">Plate</span>:
      a drawn placeholder standing in for a picture that has not been taken
      yet. Plates are captioned as such wherever they appear, so if an image
      has no caption on it, it is a photograph. Each plate comes down the
      moment there is a real frame to put in its place.
    </p>

    <h2>Placeholders</h2>
    <p>
      Anything tagged <span class="flag">Placeholder</span> is unfinished. The
      writing on those entries is a draft standing in for a real account, and
      they are marked so nobody mistakes them for something I did.
    </p>

    <h2>How it is built</h2>
    <p>
      Static HTML, one stylesheet, and no JavaScript at all. No web fonts, no
      analytics, no third-party requests of any kind. Every page is readable
      the moment the HTML arrives.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
